From 91f57cc77526ccc16e3cadd9eaef27dfddf5a43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:14:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban dashboard: refuse status writes on a card
 under another machine's live Board lease

The dashboard plugin still wrote lifecycle columns on a card another machine runs under its live Board
lease: PATCH /tasks/{id} status (drag to done/blocked/scheduled/review/ready/todo/triage), POST /tasks/bulk
status (and assignee with reclaim_first), POST /tasks/{id}/reclaim, POST /runs/{id}/terminate and
POST /tasks/{id}/reassign. Each committed locally and answered 200; the Board then rejected the status write
(live_claim) while the unfenced task_runs/task_events rows leaked to it, as the CLI did in t_01a1ccfeab615947.

Now each checks kanban_remote_stop.remote_holder() before any write. With a holder it writes nothing and
answers 409 with detail {message: kanban_remote_stop.refusal(<verb>, id, holder), holder, rejection:
live_claim, code: remote_live_lease} (the UI already renders detail.message). Bulk records a per-id
{ok: false, holder, error} and skips every op for that id; siblings still apply. Archive keeps its
stop-request route. An expired lease or this gateway's own lease behaves as before.

The helpers live in plugins/kanban/dashboard/plugin_api_remote_lease.py (plugin_api.py sits at its
2000-line cap); the dashboard _archive helper moved there too. boundary_lint baseline: the four
kanban_remote_stop imports move from plugin_api.py (2 before) to the new sibling (4): the dashboard must
call the same core guard the CLI and kanban_* tools use, there is no published plugin API for it.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_remote_lease_dashboard.py on the two-gateway fixture
(_running_on_worker) with the whole-DB _snapshot. RED before the fix: 16 failed (every PATCH status,
bulk status, reclaim/terminate/reassign answered 200 and moved the card); GREEN after: 22 passed, plus the
56 dashboard/remote-lease test files (957 passed) and scripts/check --base origin/main ok.

Card: t_01a1d4fa7525888e (follow-up of t_01a1d4df5b551228).
